---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BeforeAfter from "../../components/BeforeAfter.astro";
import Disclosure from "../../components/Disclosure.astro";
import ArrowIcon from "../../components/ArrowIcon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Hotel Enniskeen concept transformation — Mourne & Main" description="A respectful, source-backed before-and-after website concept for Enniskeen Country House Hotel in Newcastle.">
  <section class="case-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <Disclosure />
      <p class="eyebrow">Website transformation · Newcastle</p>
      <h1>Let the valley make the welcome.</h1>
      <div class="case-meta"><span>Enniskeen Country House Hotel</span><span>Concept study</span><span>20 July 2026</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="comparison-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="comparison-intro">
        <h2>Current vs concept</h2>
        <p>Drag the handle. The left shows the public opening screen captured during research; the right shows the proposed first screen.</p>
      </div>
      <BeforeAfter
        before="/images/hotel-enniskeen-current.jpg"
        after="/images/hotel-enniskeen-concept.jpg"
        beforeAlt="Enniskeen's current homepage with an archive logo, blue uppercase menu bar, photo carousel and cookie banner"
        afterAlt="Mourne and Main concept opening on the valley view from a balcony room, with the hideaway headline and an availability bar"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="design-notes" class="notes-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">The reasoning, in order</p>
      <h2>Three changes to make the stay feel closer.</h2>
      <div class="notes-grid">
        <article class="note-card">
          <span class="note-number">1</span>
          <h3>Open with the valley, not the archive</h3>
          <p>The captured page leads with an oval archive photograph, a blue serif title and seven uppercase menu items — while the hotel's own phrase, a mountainside hideaway, appears nowhere on the first screen.</p>
          <p class="note-change"><strong>Change:</strong> One composed scene — the valley framed from a balcony room, the hideaway line as the headline, and four quiet navigation items.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="note-card">
          <span class="note-number">2</span>
          <h3>Make checking dates effortless</h3>
          <p>Book Now is one menu item among seven, and checking availability means leaving for the booking engine with no dates in hand.</p>
          <p class="note-change"><strong>Change:</strong> A persistent availability bar — arrive, nights, guests — that passes straight into the hotel's existing Bookin1 engine.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="note-card">
          <span class="note-number">3</span>
          <h3>Let the estate do the selling</h3>
          <p>Twelve wooded acres, the river trail, Mourne Honey afternoon tea and the Brandy Pad Lounge are real, published draws — but they all live behind dropdown menus.</p>
          <p class="note-change"><strong>Change:</strong> The opening copy carries the estate's story in one breath, with afternoon tea one step away.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="source-section">
    <div class="shell source-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Sources &amp; limits</p>
        <h2>Clear about what is real.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>The existing-site image was captured from the public Enniskeen website on 20 July 2026, with its cookie notice left visible as a first-time visitor meets it. The hotel's name, the mountainside hideaway and Shimna Valley wording, the estate details, the phone number, the photographs and the Bookin1 booking engine all come from that site. The layout, copy hierarchy and proposed experience are independent concept work.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://www.enniskeenhotel.co.uk/" rel="external">Enniskeen public website</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.tripadvisor.co.uk/Hotel_Review-g186478-d1462012" rel="external">TripAdvisor listing used to verify current trading</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>No claim is made about sales performance, customer approval or the internal decisions behind the current site.</p>
        <a class="button" href="/request/">Request one for your business <ArrowIcon /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
